        <!-- Kodi's <texture border="N"> 9-slice crops an NxN square
             straight from the source's own corner, UNSCALED, so it only
             reads as a true radius-N corner when the source's baked radius
             equals N exactly. Too small a source radius clips the curve
             early (flatter corner); too large leaves flat filler past the
             curve. This rule was written here and nowhere else, while the
             shared capsule generator's docstring claimed one 80x80 texture
             worked at any "border=height/2", which is how every other
             capsule in the app ended up subtly wrong. Every capsule now
             uses capsule-h<height>.png with border=height/2, one asset per
             height, checked by gen_capsule_pill_assets.py:verify(). -->
